  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Let $F$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & a \\\\ 0 & a\\end{aligned}],$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The identity matrix ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $F.$\n- For the zero matrix $O$ and any $A\\in F,$ we have $A+O=A.$\n- For any $A,B\\in F,$ we have $A+B=B+A.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, every element $A$ in $F$ satisfies ${a}_{12}={a}_{11}={a}_{22},$ however, for the identity matrix ${I}_{2}$ we have ${i}_{12}=0\\ne {i}_{11}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, as for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ with real entries, we have\n\n$$\nA+O=A.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, For any matrices $A,B\\in F$ we obtain that \n\n$$\nA+B=B+A\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
